+/* Per-IB GPU profile (fuxiearly bit 16, value 16, default off; off, the ring and the fence page are exactly as without it). One job in
+ * FG_IBP_EVERY, one at a time and never with bit 27 parking, gets a CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE and a CP_REG_TO_MEM of the always-on counter
+ * (19.2 MHz) before each of its IBs and after the last, 5 ring words each, into the fence page at FG_IBP_OFF + 16*i. The stamps leave
+ * the CP thread selection as the stream has it: one Turnip command buffer can span IBs and end one inside a render pass on BR alone,
+ * and on both threads the BR write, the later one, stays. At submit each IB and the IB2s it calls are read (bounded, fault-contained,
+ * through the BO's kernel mapping) for what they do: draws, 2D blits and their area, dispatches, IB2 calls, WFIs, waits, draw-state
+ * groups, the window scissor of each render pass (its count and area), the last colour attachment 0 (RB_MRT[0] BUF_INFO and PITCH) and
+ * the last 2D destination and source. At retirement: one line per sampled job (its time per kind of IB) and its FG_IBP_TOP longest
+ * IBs; every 16 samples the time per kind over them. Diagnostic only: the WFIs serialize the IBs. */
+#define FG_IBP_OFF 1536u
+#define FG_IBP_EVERY 96u
+#define FG_IBP_TOP 6u
+#define FG_IBP_BUDGET 24576u
+#define FG_IBP_IB_BUDGET 4096u
